# PostgreSQL connection string. Locally, point this at any Postgres
# instance (a local server, or a free Neon/Vercel Postgres branch works
# fine for dev too). In production (Vercel), set this in the project's
# Environment Variables to the pooled connection string Vercel/Neon gives
# you when you add a Postgres database to the project.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/intelligence_app"

# Vercel Blob read-write token — required for the Games tab's game-video
# upload (see components/games/VideoUploadPanel.tsx). Create a Blob store
# from the Vercel project's Storage tab and connect it to this project;
# Vercel injects this variable into Production/Preview/Development
# automatically. For local development, copy that same value here (Vercel
# dashboard → Storage → your Blob store → .env.local tab), or run
# `vercel env pull` from the project root. Without it, video uploads fail
# with "Vercel Blob: Failed to retrieve the client token" — see that
# component's describeUploadError() and the upload route's server log for
# the real underlying reason.
#
# NOTE: if more than one Blob store is ever connected to the same Vercel
# project, Vercel renames the second store's vars with an extra "B"
# (BLOBB_STORE_ID / BLOBB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN) instead of overwriting the
# first store's. lib/blob-token.ts's resolveBlobReadWriteToken() checks
# both names so this works either way.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN="vercel_blob_rw_..."

